        The bug was caused by an incorrect regex pattern in the `KerberosName` class that improperly parsed Kerberos principal names, leading to incorrect assignments of the realm and host name values. This could result in failures when the application attempted to authenticate using these parsed names, particularly when handling SPNEGO (Simple and Protected GSSAPI Negotiation Mechanism) principals.

        Commit message:
        HADOOP-13890. Maintain HTTP/host as SPNEGO SPN support and
 fix KerberosName parsing. Contributed by Xiaoyu Yao.  

